From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe13 <engine@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:16:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/21] gpu: screen markers and the bottom screen at native
 size

A game can name a few small pictures it draws only in one scene ("markers":
texture format, size, screen and place). Draws that may be one are shaded on
the CPU, which says where they land; the frontend takes the markers drawn
each frame (Gpu::take_marked, Gpu::take_spans). Nothing changes for a game
with no markers: the watch is empty unless the frontend sets one.

Gpu::native_picture gives a screen's newest picture at the console's size
from the capture the hardware renderer already keeps for write-backs.

Adapted from fe-awakening-recomp 832fe86 (github.com/Zelkin1/fe-awakening-recomp,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 the authors of the Fire Emblem: Awakening
recompilation project), patches/zakuro-local-changes.patch: raster.rs
Marker/Place/MarkerWatch/marker_drawn, lib.rs marker API and native_picture,
hardware.rs native_picture/read_picture. Only the marker and readback parts
are taken; its scissor, blit-edge, texture-copy and decoding changes are not.
